+# Local Aurora entity lighting API
+
+`0.1-aurora-lighting.2` extends lighting.1 with an optional `[entity]` stage.
+This is a local fork API, not an upstream compatibility promise. Packs without
+this stage retain the stock entity pipeline; older API names reject the field.
+The manifest otherwise inherits lighting.1 (material, post and shadow requirements).
+
+```toml
+[entity]
+file = "entity.wgsl"
+name = "Model lighting"
+```
+
+The function is `fn entity(input: EntityInput) -> vec4<f32>`:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| albedo | Atlas texel times clean vertex tint, with hurt/flash overlay applied |
+| vanilla | Original fully lit colour before glint and fog; useful for fallback |
+| position | Camera-relative position in world axes, including first-person arms |
+| position_dx, position_dy | Derivatives computed before alpha discard and eligibility branches |
+| light | Normalized block light (including dynamic lights), then sky light |
+| hand | True only for the first-person pass, which follows world post-processing |
+
+Only returned RGB is used. The engine owns alpha, alpha testing, culling, glint
+and final fog. Frame is at group 3, binding 0; the existing terrain sun-shadow
+receiver is at group 2. There is no scene snapshot or cloud history binding.
+Native entity pipelines have separate world/hand override constants and use
+the original entity resources and vertex format. The two fog distances share a
+vec2 varying, leaving 15 user variables (locations 0..14) plus one built-in
+deduction for front_facing within the default limit of 16. Vertex stride and
+frame uniform ABI do not change.
+
+The hook runs on ordinary normal-shaded model vertices in the primary entity
+batch and first-person batch. Baked faces, unlit/effect overlays, particles in
+their separate pass, and explicit fullbright vertices retain vanilla lighting.
+Fullbright is identified by both original light bytes being 240 or greater;
+ordinary geometry at that exact light combination also follows the fallback.
+Item geometry with baked lighting is not relit. Specialized passes such as
+energy swirls, text and glowing outlines are unchanged.
+
+This adds shadow reception, not entity shadow casting. Terrain shadow casters
+are unchanged. Pack fallback remains necessary for other dimensions and visual
+effects. A pack must account for the hand being drawn after the world post chain.
+
+## Validation
+
+- Shader API test verifies opt-in gating, inclusion in the archive and no scene snapshot.
+- Developer composition harness validates an actual pack against the full entity WGSL.
+- `entity_interstage_contract_fits_default_limits` checks the actual fragment
+  interface against default wgpu limits, including built-in deductions. It
+  reproduces the first Metal launch failure (16 user variables plus front_facing)
+  before the fog-distance packing fix and passes afterwards, without a GPU.
+- `gfx::native_entity::gpu_tests::model_hook_contract_on_gpu` renders and reads
+  back normal/hand, baked, fullbright, hurt, item glint, armour glint, unlit and
+  transparent cases. Set `AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1` to fail instead of skipping when
+  no adapter is available.
+- `local_pack_pipelines_on_gpu` now builds both entity variants as part of the
+  actual pack. Run with `HORIZON_VALIDATE_SHADER_PACK=<archive>` and `--ignored`.
+
+The first Terminal run passed four shadow tests and temporal history on Apple M3
+Pro / Metal, then failed at entity pipeline creation due to the interface limit.
+The corrected model contract and whole-pack hardware tests await the next
+Terminal run; the agent environment has no Metal adapter. In-world acceptance
+is still pending.
